      "message": "How do you make sure the hidden key ladder registers that the are inputs to cert 8 have the right values here?\nTypically one has to rerun the key ladder from the start, every time..\n\nAlso, cert 8 is low down the ladder, does not depend on FRK etc. Is that what we want?\n\nTo be sure we\u0027re talking about the same mechanics: a single key_ladder_step is a single hmac-sha256 on two inputs. There are hidden registers like isr0, isr1, .. One needs to call the key_ladder_steps in the right order to get consistent derived values.\n\nI was thinking more something like we store master seed,\nderive rsa from hmac(seed, \"rsa\") and we share that derived seed w/ CA.\nAnd we generate ecc with hmac(seed, \"ecc\") and not share that derived seed, just the public key. And not share the master seed.",
